67
00:03:07,646 --> 00:03:09,940
Well, yeah, I just wanna make
a few extra bucks.

68
00:03:10,024 --> 00:03:11,025
What's the big deal?

69
00:03:11,609 --> 00:03:12,610
Well, uh...

70
00:03:13,694 --> 00:03:15,821
We agreed we needed a family day.

71
00:03:15,905 --> 00:03:17,323
And now, you're leaving.

72
00:03:17,406 --> 00:03:19,783
Uh, and we agreed that
Starbuck should stay home.

73
00:03:19,867 --> 00:03:21,493
And then you told Brian
he could bring him.

74
00:03:21,577 --> 00:03:23,787
Yeah, well, just let
the boy hang out with his dog.

75
00:03:26,206 --> 00:03:27,458
Can we talk for a minute?

76
00:03:35,090 --> 00:03:37,134
Mom and Dad are fighting again.

77
00:03:38,761 --> 00:03:42,056
Do you think they're ever gonna get a...

78
00:03:43,724 --> 00:03:44,850
No.

79
00:03:45,851 --> 00:03:47,227
No, they wouldn't do that.

80
00:03:51,065 --> 00:03:53,067
How long are we gonna keep
putting off the conversation?

81
00:03:53,150 --> 00:03:54,568
Oh, can't we just enjoy the weekend?

82
00:03:54,652 --> 00:03:55,986
It's not working.

83
00:03:57,529 --> 00:03:59,698
The kids can feel it.
Brian's already acting out.

84
00:03:59,782 --> 00:04:00,908
He's just being a 13-year-old.

85
00:04:00,991 --> 00:04:01,825
Greg, stop doing that.

86
00:04:01,909 --> 00:04:03,869
- Doing what?
- Ignoring the problem.

87
00:04:05,412 --> 00:04:06,622
It's a beautiful day, isn't it?

88
00:04:06,705 --> 00:04:07,873
Yes, it is.

89
00:04:09,458 --> 00:04:10,834
Look, I-- I gotta go.

90
00:04:10,918 --> 00:04:12,503
I-- I'll see you tonight.

91
00:04:19,301 --> 00:04:21,679
<i>Star player
Lance Parrish had two hits</i>

92
00:04:21,762 --> 00:04:24,098
<i>despite the Tigers losing to the Rangers.</i>

93
00:04:24,181 --> 00:04:27,393
<i>And speaking of stars,
NASA is still tracking</i>

94
00:04:27,476 --> 00:04:30,104
<i>a series of unusual ripples in space</i>

95
00:04:30,187 --> 00:04:31,146
<i>coming off an unprecedented wave</i>...

96
00:04:31,230 --> 00:04:32,314
That is so sweet of you.

97
00:04:32,398 --> 00:04:33,816
- <i>...of solar flares.</i>
- Come on inside.

98
00:04:33,899 --> 00:04:35,442
<i>Due to this activ--</i>

99
00:04:35,526 --> 00:04:37,403
Have you told your husband
about your book?

100
00:04:38,529 --> 00:04:39,530
No.

101
00:04:40,030 --> 00:04:41,657
No.

102
00:04:41,740 --> 00:04:43,033
I don't think he'd appreciate it.

103
00:04:43,117 --> 00:04:45,160
Well, that's a shame.

104
00:04:46,370 --> 00:04:49,206
I love what you've written so far.

105
00:04:49,873 --> 00:04:51,000
Thank you.

106
00:04:51,083 --> 00:04:53,794
It's hard to describe how much
this surprised me.

107
00:04:53,877 --> 00:04:55,629
I would never have guessed

108
00:04:55,713 --> 00:04:58,590
that you could write something so intense.

109
00:04:58,674 --> 00:05:01,260
Well, I mean, it's not really me.

110
00:05:01,343 --> 00:05:03,095
It's-It's just a story.

111
00:05:03,178 --> 00:05:07,141
Well, I love some of the little details.

112
00:05:08,183 --> 00:05:09,643
Like the fact that she always

113
00:05:09,727 --> 00:05:11,979
keeps her yellow suitcase packed.

114
00:05:12,062 --> 00:05:13,522
Ready to leave for New York

115
00:05:13,605 --> 00:05:15,691
the minute she gets up the nerve to do it.

116
00:05:15,774 --> 00:05:18,027
And that scene

117
00:05:18,110 --> 00:05:20,821
where she's holding
the suitcase in her arms,

118
00:05:20,904 --> 00:05:23,365
and cries while she watches her children

119
00:05:23,449 --> 00:05:24,742
playing in the yard

120
00:05:24,825 --> 00:05:28,537
is heartbreaking and beautifully written.

121
00:05:31,206 --> 00:05:33,709
Thank you.

122
00:05:33,792 --> 00:05:36,128
I'd like to read the next
draft when you're finished.

123
00:05:36,211 --> 00:05:38,756
Are you sure? You have been
so generous with your time.

124
00:05:38,839 --> 00:05:40,132
I-I feel bad.

125
00:05:40,215 --> 00:05:44,303
Denise, I edited my husband's
work for 40 years

126
00:05:44,386 --> 00:05:45,846
without a lot of gratitude.

127
00:05:45,929 --> 00:05:48,932
I'm more than happy
to give some editorial advice

128
00:05:49,016 --> 00:05:51,060
to someone who cares.

129
00:05:51,143 --> 00:05:52,186
Well, thank you so much.

130
00:05:52,269 --> 00:05:54,271
I-I can't tell you
how much I appreciate it.

131
00:05:54,354 --> 00:05:56,857
Oh. Do you have a minute?

132
00:05:56,940 --> 00:05:58,108
Sure.

133
00:05:58,192 --> 00:06:00,819
