215
00:09:41,915 --> 00:09:43,583
I got us a pizza for dinner.

216
00:09:45,127 --> 00:09:46,628
Great. I'm starving.

217
00:09:46,712 --> 00:09:48,088
Well, there's plenty to eat.

218
00:09:49,381 --> 00:09:51,258
Why do we gotta take this thing off?

219
00:09:51,341 --> 00:09:52,843
Wouldn't it just be easier
to leave it on all the time?

220
00:09:52,926 --> 00:09:54,803
Yeah, it embarrasses your mother.

221
00:09:54,886 --> 00:09:56,471
Oh.

222
00:10:00,892 --> 00:10:02,686
You're gonna stop
with the cigarettes, right?

223
00:10:04,313 --> 00:10:05,397
I don't smoke.

224
00:10:05,480 --> 00:10:06,982
- Don't lie to me, Brian.
- I'm not.

225
00:10:07,065 --> 00:10:08,567
I can smell it on you.

226
00:10:10,319 --> 00:10:11,445
Sorry, Dad.

227
00:10:11,528 --> 00:10:13,530
- What's with you anyway?
- Nothing.

228
00:10:13,613 --> 00:10:14,906
Trying to impress somebody?

229
00:10:14,990 --> 00:10:16,450
No.

230
00:10:16,533 --> 00:10:17,492
That crap is the reason

231
00:10:17,576 --> 00:10:18,910
your grandpa got his vocal cords cut out.

232
00:10:18,994 --> 00:10:20,412
You don't want cancer, do you?

233
00:10:21,830 --> 00:10:23,373
Uh-uh.

234
00:10:23,457 --> 00:10:25,125
All right. Let's put this
stupid thing in the garage

235
00:10:25,208 --> 00:10:26,543
where your mother can't see it.

236
00:10:31,798 --> 00:10:33,550
I was like, "Hold on."

237
00:10:35,427 --> 00:10:36,428
What was that?

238
00:10:36,511 --> 00:10:38,055
I have no idea.

239
00:10:38,138 --> 00:10:39,806
Mel's really getting to be a problem.

240
00:10:39,890 --> 00:10:41,266
He threatened the dog today.

241
00:10:41,350 --> 00:10:42,851
Wait, what? He better not hurt Starbuck.

242
00:10:42,934 --> 00:10:44,311
No, no, no. Nobody's gonna hurt the dog.

243
00:10:44,394 --> 00:10:45,228
Hey, Starbuck.

244
00:10:45,312 --> 00:10:46,480
This is Mel's head.

245
00:10:46,563 --> 00:10:47,647
You want to bite it, right?

246
00:10:47,731 --> 00:10:49,691
No, no, that's not his head.
That's his balls.

247
00:10:49,775 --> 00:10:51,234
Yeah, Starbuck.

248
00:10:51,318 --> 00:10:53,528
- Here's Mel's testicles.
- Good boy. Get his--

249
00:10:53,612 --> 00:10:55,197
Oh. Okay. Good boy. You want to go get it?

250
00:10:55,280 --> 00:10:56,948
- Come on, get his balls.
- Go get him!

251
00:10:57,032 --> 00:10:58,283
Yay!

252
00:10:58,367 --> 00:10:59,451
He's chomping on them.

253
00:10:59,534 --> 00:11:00,952
That's what he's gonna do to Mel's balls.

254
00:11:01,036 --> 00:11:02,746
Dad, tell Brian to keep his
mouth shut while he's eating.

255
00:11:02,829 --> 00:11:03,997
It's so gross.

256
00:11:04,081 --> 00:11:06,917
Don't talk when you've got
food in your mouth, Brian.

257
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:07,876
Ew.

258
00:11:07,959 --> 00:11:09,211
- Mom, he's been so gross...
- Mm-hmm.

259
00:11:09,294 --> 00:11:10,754
...since the time he was a little boy.

260
00:11:10,837 --> 00:11:12,631
Do you remember
when he pooped in the bath?

261
00:11:12,714 --> 00:11:14,049
Okay, that was a little poop.

262
00:11:14,132 --> 00:11:15,175
No. No, it wasn't.

263
00:11:15,258 --> 00:11:17,010
No, she's right.
It was a lot of poop.

264
00:11:17,094 --> 00:11:19,137
Okay... so what? What?

265
00:11:19,221 --> 00:11:20,597
I was just like four years old
or something.

266
00:11:20,680 --> 00:11:22,015
Uh-uh.

267
00:11:42,536 --> 00:11:44,871
<i>Now were you or were you not
on the night of June the 13th</i>

268
00:11:44,955 --> 00:11:47,457
<i>in Mrs. Throttlebottom's chicken coop?</i>

269
00:11:47,541 --> 00:11:49,292
<i>Soitenly not! I was in the house!</i>

270
00:11:49,376 --> 00:11:50,961
<i>- What house?
- The doghouse.</i>

271
00:11:51,044 --> 00:11:52,295
<i>Nyuk, nyuk, nyuk, nyuk!</i>

272
00:13:00,572 --> 00:13:01,990
Hey, boy. You're all wet.

273
00:13:07,537 --> 00:13:08,622
Good boy.

274
00:13:13,126 --> 00:13:14,336
What did you see?

275
00:13:25,305 --> 00:13:27,057
Did anybody else
see that weird light

276
00:13:27,140 --> 00:13:28,642
in the backyard last night?

277
00:13:28,725 --> 00:13:30,602
- What weird light?
- <i>The Chicago White Sox...</i>

278
00:13:30,685 --> 00:13:31,853
I don't know where it came from,

279
00:13:31,937 --> 00:13:34,481
but Starbuck was all
freaked out and barking.

280
00:13:34,564 --> 00:13:35,857
Oh, great. That's all we need.

281
00:13:35,941 --> 00:13:37,067
What did it look like?

282
00:13:38,276 --> 00:13:40,320
Well, there was a light coming
through the window.

283
00:13:40,403 --> 00:13:42,822
It was really bright. It flickered.

284
00:13:42,906 --> 00:13:45,200
And then the wind was blowing all crazy.

285
00:13:45,283 --> 00:13:46,910
And then it was gone.

286
00:13:46,993 --> 00:13:48,828
Could have been lights from a helicopter.

287
00:13:48,912 --> 00:13:50,288
Or a UFO.

288
00:13:50,372 --> 00:13:51,373
Aliens.

289
00:13:51,456 --> 00:13:52,624
Shut up, Dad.

290
00:13:52,707 --> 00:13:53,917
How long was he barking for?

291
00:13:54,668 --> 00:13:56,503
Long enough to wake me up.

292
00:14:01,258 --> 00:14:02,342
Hey, Mel, what's going on?

293
00:14:02,425 --> 00:14:03,677
Nothing good.

294
00:14:03,760 --> 00:14:05,804
Kids pulled off one hell
of a prank last night.

295
00:14:06,596 --> 00:14:07,430
What happened?

296
00:14:07,514 --> 00:14:08,515
They didn't do anything to you.

297
00:14:08,598 --> 00:14:09,516
Oh, you gotta see it.

298
00:14:09,599 --> 00:14:10,600
It's gonna take me all day to clean up.

299
00:14:10,684 --> 00:14:13,103
Hey, Mel, what--
what are you talking about?

300
00:14:13,186 --> 00:14:15,814
No, no, come on. Come take a look, Greg.

301
00:14:18,984 --> 00:14:20,819
All right.

302
00:14:22,904 --> 00:14:23,905
Holy shit.

303
00:14:23,989 --> 00:14:25,782
Yes, yes, that is exactly what that is.

304
00:14:25,865 --> 00:14:28,076
That is about a couple
hundred pounds of cow manure.

305
00:14:28,827 --> 00:14:30,412
You think my kids did this?

306
00:14:30,495 --> 00:14:32,330
Either them...

307
00:14:32,414 --> 00:14:33,456
Or your wife.

308
00:14:33,540 --> 00:14:35,250
Oh, come on now, Mel. Really?

309
00:14:36,418 --> 00:14:37,794
- You see, I knew it.
- Hey. Brian. Audrey.

310
00:14:37,877 --> 00:14:39,421
- I knew they did it. Damn it.
- Stop laughing.

311
00:14:39,504 --> 00:14:40,338
I knew it.

312
00:14:40,422 --> 00:14:41,381
Look, they just think it's funny

313
00:14:41,464 --> 00:14:43,967
because it's, uh...

314
00:14:44,050 --> 00:14:45,969
I promise you, my family
had nothing to do with this.

315
00:14:46,052 --> 00:14:47,220
Greg, please. Okay.

316
00:14:47,304 --> 00:14:49,848
If it wasn't them,
then who else did this, huh?

317
00:14:49,931 --> 00:14:52,225
You're the only neighbors
I'm having trouble with.

318
00:14:52,309 --> 00:14:53,560
I have no idea.

319
00:14:53,643 --> 00:14:56,730
But if you need help cleaning
it up, then I'll be here.

320
00:14:56,813 --> 00:14:58,481
And Brian can help, too.

321
00:14:58,565 --> 00:14:59,649
What?

322
00:15:02,444 --> 00:15:05,071
- Thank you, Greg.
- Come on, man.

323
00:15:05,155 --> 00:15:06,573
- I appreciate it.
- All right.

324
00:15:25,884 --> 00:15:27,385
Denise, it's so nice to see you.

325
00:15:27,469 --> 00:15:30,096
Good to see you, Mrs. Valcourt.

326
00:15:30,180 --> 00:15:32,474
I was wondering if you could
help me out with something.

327
00:15:32,557 --> 00:15:33,892
Oh. Yes, what do you need?

328
00:15:33,975 --> 00:15:37,312
Mrs. Huddleston found
this plant in her backyard,

329
00:15:37,395 --> 00:15:39,314
and we're trying to figure out what it is.

330
00:15:39,397 --> 00:15:40,774
Now, I looked through all of these books,

331
00:15:40,857 --> 00:15:42,025
but I can't find anything like it.

332
00:15:42,108 --> 00:15:43,610
Do you have any idea what it could be?

333
00:15:43,693 --> 00:15:46,404
It's funny. It looks a lot
like Pleuromeia.

334
00:15:47,405 --> 00:15:50,283
Uh, Pleuro... What's that?

335
00:15:50,367 --> 00:15:51,660
It can't be Pleuromeia,

336
00:15:51,743 --> 00:15:53,620
because that species has been extinct

337
00:15:53,703 --> 00:15:55,705
for over 200 million years.

338
00:15:55,789 --> 00:15:57,624
- 200 million years?
- Yes.

339
00:16:00,001 --> 00:16:02,087
I'll tell Mrs. Huddleston.
She'll get a kick out of that.

340
00:16:02,170 --> 00:16:03,505
I'm sorry I couldn't help you more.

341
00:16:03,588 --> 00:16:04,589
Hmm.

342
00:16:09,969 --> 00:16:11,346
I like your new bike.

343
00:16:11,429 --> 00:16:12,931
Thanks. I mean, the handlebars
are pretty cool.

344
00:16:13,014 --> 00:16:14,849
I customized them a few days ago.

345
00:16:14,933 --> 00:16:17,268
My bike is all black.
I need a new one.

346
00:16:17,352 --> 00:16:19,062
Yeah, this one's, like, red,
and blue. It's pretty cool.

347
00:16:19,145 --> 00:16:20,188
You think maybe I should get it, too?

348
00:16:20,271 --> 00:16:21,272
I think you'll like it.

349
00:16:21,356 --> 00:16:22,440
Wait! Brian!

350
00:16:22,524 --> 00:16:23,525
It's Kaden Tucker!

351
00:16:23,608 --> 00:16:25,443
- Oh, shit!
- Go, go, go, go!

352
00:16:25,527 --> 00:16:28,655
Brian Platt! Get back here!
I'm gonna kick your ass!

353
00:16:28,738 --> 00:16:29,823
You're dead!

354
00:16:29,906 --> 00:16:31,241
Come on! Let's get him!

355
00:16:32,158 --> 00:16:33,410
- Get him!
- Let's go!

356
00:16:34,744 --> 00:16:35,829
Oh, shit!

357
00:16:43,628 --> 00:16:45,130
Where are you, Brian?

358
00:16:45,213 --> 00:16:46,297
No point in hiding.

359
00:16:46,965 --> 00:16:48,299
Come here, Brian!

360
00:16:49,050 --> 00:16:50,719
Come out, bitchsqueak!

361
00:16:50,802 --> 00:16:52,387
You broke my brother's arm!

362
00:16:52,470 --> 00:16:54,222
Just you wait till we find you, Platt!

363
00:16:54,764 --> 00:16:56,266
Brian!

364
00:16:56,349 --> 00:16:58,143
We're coming for you, Brian!

365
00:16:58,226 --> 00:16:59,853
Come out, come out,
wherever you are!

366
00:17:00,979 --> 00:17:02,355
You're done, Platt!

367
00:17:03,231 --> 00:17:04,733
Let's go left. We'll find him.

368
00:17:12,657 --> 00:17:13,658
Thank you.

369
00:17:13,742 --> 00:17:15,243
You're welcome. Thanks. Good night.

370
00:17:26,421 --> 00:17:28,131
<i>Right next to his hand.</i>

371
00:17:28,214 --> 00:17:29,382
<i>Let's drink it.</i>

372
00:17:29,466 --> 00:17:31,134
<i>Yeah, let's get drunk.</i>

373
00:17:31,217 --> 00:17:33,887
<i>Man, you can't get drunk
on one can of beer.</i>

374
00:18:15,512 --> 00:18:16,513
Mom!

375
00:18:16,596 --> 00:18:17,597
Dad!

376
00:18:24,521 --> 00:18:25,980
The power's out again.

377
00:18:27,649 --> 00:18:28,691
What was that noise?

378
00:18:28,775 --> 00:18:30,568
It felt like my eardrums popped.

379
00:18:31,486 --> 00:18:32,821
Denise? Kids?

380
00:18:32,904 --> 00:18:34,823
Could have been lightning
striking a transformer.

381
00:18:34,906 --> 00:18:36,157
I don't know.

382
00:18:36,241 --> 00:18:37,575
The clock's dead.

383
00:18:37,659 --> 00:18:38,868
Must have happened just past 11.

384
00:18:38,952 --> 00:18:40,620
- Everybody all right?
- Yeah, Dad, we're fine.

385
00:18:40,703 --> 00:18:41,955
Did you guys see that lightning?

386
00:18:42,038 --> 00:18:43,790
Yeah, it was bright as hell.

387
00:18:43,873 --> 00:18:46,209
The whole sky lit up just like that.

388
00:18:46,292 --> 00:18:48,044
- Where's Mom at?
- I don't know.

389
00:18:48,127 --> 00:18:49,420
Denise, you downstairs?

390
00:18:49,504 --> 00:18:50,505
Yes.

391
00:18:52,382 --> 00:18:53,633
I'm here.

392
00:18:53,716 --> 00:18:54,801
Everybody okay?

393
00:18:54,884 --> 00:18:55,927
Yeah, we're all fine.

394
00:18:56,010 --> 00:18:57,428
Just a little startled, I guess.

395
00:18:57,512 --> 00:18:58,888
What were you doing in the basement?

396
00:18:58,972 --> 00:19:02,517
Huh? Laundry.
Washing your dirty underpants.

397
00:19:02,600 --> 00:19:03,768
Funny, Mom.

398
00:19:03,852 --> 00:19:05,937
My ears are popping like
I just flew in an airplane.

399
00:19:06,020 --> 00:19:07,355
Yeah, mine too.

400
00:19:07,438 --> 00:19:08,815
That doesn't make sense.

401
00:19:08,898 --> 00:19:10,692
What would cause
that type of pressure change?

402
00:19:10,775 --> 00:19:11,776
Yeah, it looks like

403
00:19:11,860 --> 00:19:13,611
the whole neighborhood's lost power.

404
00:19:13,695 --> 00:19:15,113
Phone lines are down.

405
00:19:15,196 --> 00:19:17,282
- Shit.
- Watch your language, Audrey.

406
00:19:17,365 --> 00:19:19,826
Mom, I'm hungry.
Can I get something to eat?

407
00:19:19,909 --> 00:19:21,160
Huh? Yeah.

408
00:19:21,244 --> 00:19:22,829
- Only from the cupboard.
- Okay.

409
00:19:22,912 --> 00:19:23,830
Nobody's opening the fridge

410
00:19:23,913 --> 00:19:24,831
until the power comes back on.

411
00:19:24,914 --> 00:19:26,457
I don't want all that food to go bad.

412
00:19:28,334 --> 00:19:29,752
Did anyone else notice?

413
00:19:30,920 --> 00:19:32,130
The rain stopped.

414
00:19:32,922 --> 00:19:34,257
There's no more thunder.

415
00:19:37,802 --> 00:19:38,970
Yeah, it's quiet.

416
00:19:40,555 --> 00:19:42,098
I think we should all
try and get some sleep,

417
00:19:42,181 --> 00:19:43,683
and hopefully by the time we wake up,

418
00:19:43,766 --> 00:19:44,851
the power will be back on.

419
00:19:47,437 --> 00:19:48,646
- The hell was that?
- Shh.

420
00:19:48,730 --> 00:19:50,064
- Quiet.
- Someone's hurt.

421
00:19:51,566 --> 00:19:52,775
Brian, give me your flashlight.

422
00:19:53,443 --> 00:19:54,485
Wait, no, no, no, Dad.

423
00:19:54,569 --> 00:19:55,612
- Greg.
- What?

424
00:19:55,695 --> 00:19:56,946
I don't think you should go out there.

425
00:19:57,030 --> 00:19:59,115
Well, someone might need help.
Just stay inside, please.

426
00:20:15,465 --> 00:20:16,549
Hello?

427
00:20:33,983 --> 00:20:35,860
Brian, make sure the back door is locked.

428
00:20:35,944 --> 00:20:37,403
- And-And check on the dog.
- Check on the dog.

429
00:20:37,487 --> 00:20:39,656
- Dad, what is happening?
- I don't know.

430
00:20:39,739 --> 00:20:41,574
I think we should stay inside
the house until morning.

431
00:20:41,658 --> 00:20:42,909
There could be power lines down.

432
00:20:42,992 --> 00:20:44,452
I don't know how dangerous
it is out there.

433
00:20:44,535 --> 00:20:45,954
What about the people who were screaming?

434
00:20:46,037 --> 00:20:46,913
Don't they need help?

435
00:20:46,996 --> 00:20:48,122
I don't know who those people are,

436
00:20:48,206 --> 00:20:49,582
but the police will be there to help them.

437
00:20:49,666 --> 00:20:51,250
Back door is locked.
Starbuck's in his doghouse.

438
00:20:51,334 --> 00:20:52,669
- What about the police?
- Thank you, buddy.

439
00:20:52,752 --> 00:20:53,962
Shouldn't we be hearing sirens?

440
00:20:54,045 --> 00:20:55,546
Audrey, stop it. Are you
trying to scare your brother?

441
00:20:55,630 --> 00:20:58,049
No, I'm not. I'm just trying to figure out
what's happening.

442
00:20:58,132 --> 00:20:59,676
Why don't you get some pillows
and blankets,

443
00:20:59,759 --> 00:21:01,135
and we'll all sleep in the family room.

444
00:21:01,219 --> 00:21:02,387
- That's a good idea.
- All together.

445
00:21:02,470 --> 00:21:04,138
Good idea.
Come on. Go get your stuff.

446
00:21:06,849 --> 00:21:08,267
Just a regular slumber party.

447
00:21:11,896 --> 00:21:13,606
Okay, I... [stutters] ...I'll get some snacks.

448
00:21:13,690 --> 00:21:15,108
- I'll get the blankets.
- Yeah.

449
00:22:03,656 --> 00:22:05,074
Still no power?

450
00:22:07,744 --> 00:22:08,786
Nope.

451
00:22:09,328 --> 00:22:10,413
Sucks.

452
00:22:11,664 --> 00:22:13,666
I wanna watch MTV.

453
00:22:13,750 --> 00:22:15,251
We'll get it on soon.

454
00:22:18,337 --> 00:22:20,256
Why is it so warm in here?

455
00:22:20,339 --> 00:22:21,632
I'll open some windows.

456
00:22:27,805 --> 00:22:30,224
- Greg?
- Yeah?

457
00:22:30,308 --> 00:22:31,309
Starbuck got out again.

458
00:22:31,392 --> 00:22:32,560
- How?
- I don't know.

459
00:22:32,643 --> 00:22:35,354
He must have broken his leash
and dug under the fence.

460
00:22:36,647 --> 00:22:37,774
Can I go looking for him?

461
00:22:37,857 --> 00:22:39,567
No, no, not just yet.

462
00:22:39,650 --> 00:22:41,360
I told you there could be power lines down

463
00:22:41,444 --> 00:22:42,695
in the street.

464
00:22:42,779 --> 00:22:45,656
Dad, I'm not stupid.
I'm not gonna grab onto one.

465
00:22:45,740 --> 00:22:47,825
Hey, should we drink the milk
before it goes bad?

466
00:22:47,909 --> 00:22:48,743
Mm-hmm.

467
00:22:48,826 --> 00:22:49,827
Everybody want cereal?

468
00:22:49,911 --> 00:22:50,912
- Yes, please.
- Yeah.

469
00:22:50,995 --> 00:22:52,121
Yeah.

470
00:22:55,333 --> 00:22:56,417
Thank you.

471
00:22:58,002 --> 00:22:59,921
You staying home today?

472
00:23:00,004 --> 00:23:02,965
No. No, I can go in a little late.

473
00:23:03,049 --> 00:23:04,383
I'll tell them about the power.

474
00:23:04,467 --> 00:23:06,010
- They'll understand.
- Okay.

475
00:23:08,096 --> 00:23:09,514
I'll go find Starbuck.

476
00:23:09,597 --> 00:23:11,516
And see what kind of damage
the storm caused.

477
00:23:11,599 --> 00:23:13,768
I just hope Mel didn't
do anything to him.

478
00:23:13,851 --> 00:23:15,144
No, no.

479
00:23:15,228 --> 00:23:16,896
He's probably
in the MacAllisters' backyard

480
00:23:16,979 --> 00:23:19,190
trying to get fresh with
that pretty little dachshund.

481
00:23:19,273 --> 00:23:20,650
- Gross, Dad.
- What?

482
00:23:20,733 --> 00:23:21,901
Why don't we go together?

483
00:23:21,984 --> 00:23:23,319
I wanna check on Mrs. Huddleston,

484
00:23:23,402 --> 00:23:24,445
make sure she's okay.

485
00:23:24,529 --> 00:23:26,739
Yeah. All right, let's do that.

486
00:23:26,823 --> 00:23:29,200
You two, stay inside
until your mom and I get back.

487
00:23:29,283 --> 00:23:30,535
- Sure.
- Mm-hmm.

488
00:23:30,618 --> 00:23:32,078
Brian,

489
00:23:32,161 --> 00:23:33,454
Kaden Tucker came by yesterday.

490
00:23:33,538 --> 00:23:35,039
He was looking for you.

491
00:23:35,123 --> 00:23:36,124
Don't tell him I'm here.

492
00:23:36,207 --> 00:23:37,208
Damn it.

493
00:23:37,291 --> 00:23:38,376
Water's not working.

494
00:23:38,459 --> 00:23:39,836
Oh, the main line must have burst.

495
00:23:39,919 --> 00:23:41,212
That was one hell of a storm.

496
00:23:41,295 --> 00:23:42,755
Are there any utilities left to break?

497
00:23:42,839 --> 00:23:44,173
No, we got 'em all.

498
00:23:44,257 --> 00:23:45,174
Good.

499
00:23:51,055 --> 00:23:52,598
Lock the door behind us, okay?

500
00:23:52,682 --> 00:23:53,808
Yeah, Mom.

501
00:24:04,735 --> 00:24:05,820
Oof.

502
00:24:09,031 --> 00:24:10,032
It's hot.

503
00:24:10,116 --> 00:24:11,200
Yeah.

504
00:24:12,869 --> 00:24:13,911
Starbuck!

505
00:24:25,882 --> 00:24:27,049
Do you hear that?

506
00:24:28,092 --> 00:24:29,093
Yeah.

507
00:24:49,030 --> 00:24:50,698
That explains the water being out.

508
00:24:52,533 --> 00:24:54,493
No, I don't think so.

509
00:24:54,577 --> 00:24:56,204
That's not a burst pipe.

510
00:24:57,705 --> 00:24:59,415
That water is steaming hot.

511
00:25:05,838 --> 00:25:07,089
I'm gonna cut through the yards,

512
00:25:07,173 --> 00:25:09,175
head over to the next block,
see if they have power.

513
00:25:09,258 --> 00:25:10,468
I have a feeling that Starbuck's

514
00:25:10,551 --> 00:25:12,220
in the MacAllisters' backyard.

515
00:25:12,303 --> 00:25:13,137
Okay.

516
00:25:13,221 --> 00:25:14,305
Meet you back at the house.

517
00:25:18,100 --> 00:25:19,352
Starbuck!

518
00:26:18,953 --> 00:26:19,954
Mrs. Huddleston?

519
00:26:25,001 --> 00:26:26,002
Mrs. Huddleston?

520
00:26:38,806 --> 00:26:39,807
Hello?

521
00:26:41,684 --> 00:26:42,768
Mrs. Huddleston?

522
00:27:14,133 --> 00:27:15,217
What the hell?

523
00:27:16,510 --> 00:27:17,511
Brian!

524
00:27:18,387 --> 00:27:20,514
Brian! Come here, quick!

525
00:27:30,649 --> 00:27:31,942
Starbuck!

526
00:27:37,531 --> 00:27:38,741
Mrs. Huddleston?

527
00:27:44,538 --> 00:27:45,664
Mrs. Huddleston?

528
00:27:46,999 --> 00:27:48,000
Mrs...

529
00:27:50,669 --> 00:27:52,588
Oh, God, Mrs. Huddleston.

530
00:27:52,671 --> 00:27:53,798
Mrs. Huddleston.

531
00:28:06,435 --> 00:28:07,436
Holy Jesus.

532
00:28:09,105 --> 00:28:10,106
Oh, God.

533
00:28:11,273 --> 00:28:12,608
Holy Jesus.

534
00:29:01,615 --> 00:29:04,243
Brian! Brian, get up here!

535
00:29:04,326 --> 00:29:05,828
What's going on? Why are you yelling?

536
00:29:05,911 --> 00:29:08,622
- I saw something. It was big.
- What'd you see?

537
00:29:08,706 --> 00:29:10,583
And it looked like it was
moving in this direction.

538
00:29:10,666 --> 00:29:13,294
- What was it, an animal?
- I don't know.

539
00:29:13,377 --> 00:29:14,587
Did an elephant escape from the zoo?

540
00:29:14,670 --> 00:29:16,714
It wasn't a damn elephant!

541
00:29:16,797 --> 00:29:18,007
Are you sure you saw something?

542
00:29:18,090 --> 00:29:19,675
- Stop it, Brian! I did.
- Okay, okay,

543
00:29:19,758 --> 00:29:20,885
but you're freaking me out.

544
00:29:37,902 --> 00:29:38,903
Starbuck?

545
00:31:26,760 --> 00:31:28,220
- Come on! Let's go!
- What?

546
00:31:28,304 --> 00:31:29,930
Let's go!

547
00:31:36,854 --> 00:31:38,063
Oh, my God! He's gaining!

548
00:31:38,147 --> 00:31:39,690
Run, Denise!

549
00:31:41,442 --> 00:31:42,526
What the hell's going on?

550
00:31:42,610 --> 00:31:44,486
- No! No!
- Get inside now!

551
00:31:44,570 --> 00:31:46,113
- Get inside!
- I just heard a gunshot.

552
00:31:47,615 --> 00:31:48,657
I can do it.

553
00:31:50,159 --> 00:31:53,245
<i>♪ Flintstones
Meet the Flintstones ♪</i>

554
00:31:53,329 --> 00:31:54,496
- Mom, you put her in?
- Yeah, I got it.

555
00:31:54,580 --> 00:31:57,958
♪<i>They're the modern
Stone-age family ♪</i>

556
00:31:58,042 --> 00:31:59,501
Keep moving. Keep going.

557
00:31:59,585 --> 00:32:03,047
<i>♪ When you're
With the Flintstones ♪</i>

558
00:32:03,130 --> 00:32:05,883
<i>♪ Have a
Yabba-dabba-doo time ♪</i>

559
00:32:12,681 --> 00:32:14,266
Audrey, open the door!

560
00:32:14,350 --> 00:32:15,684
- Brian!
- Okay.

561
00:32:15,768 --> 00:32:17,227
- Audrey, come on!
- Open the door!

562
00:32:18,145 --> 00:32:19,146
Audrey!

563
00:32:20,939 --> 00:32:22,274
Mom, look!

564
00:32:22,816 --> 00:32:23,859
Audrey!

565
00:32:23,942 --> 00:32:25,486
Brian!

566
00:32:26,904 --> 00:32:27,988
Oh, God!

567
00:32:28,072 --> 00:32:29,907
Brian! Audrey! Open the door!

568
00:32:29,990 --> 00:32:31,367
Oh, my God. What is that?

569
00:32:33,452 --> 00:32:34,703
Open the door, quick!

570
00:32:35,621 --> 00:32:37,706
Oh, my God! Quick!

571
00:32:37,790 --> 00:32:39,208
Brian!

572
00:32:41,543 --> 00:32:43,337
- Go!
- Shit.

573
00:32:48,801 --> 00:32:51,261
What is that? What is that?

574
00:32:51,345 --> 00:32:52,930
Mom! Mom.

575
00:32:53,013 --> 00:32:55,307
Mom!

576
00:33:03,023 --> 00:33:04,358
Dad. Dad.

577
00:33:07,653 --> 00:33:09,071
Oh, my God.

578
00:33:21,166 --> 00:33:23,919
I think-- I think-- I think they're gone.

579
00:33:24,002 --> 00:33:26,338
What's happening?

580
00:33:26,422 --> 00:33:28,716
- I don't know.
- What was at the door?

581
00:33:28,799 --> 00:33:30,467
- Dad, what was that?
- We've got to get out of here.

582
00:33:30,551 --> 00:33:31,802
- Why don't we get in the car?
- Yeah.

583
00:33:31,885 --> 00:33:32,803
Go to my parents' house.

584
00:33:32,886 --> 00:33:33,887
Maybe this isn't happening in Chicago.

585
00:33:33,971 --> 00:33:35,097
- That's a good idea.
- Dad, are we gonna die?

586
00:33:35,180 --> 00:33:36,181
No, no, no!

587
00:33:36,265 --> 00:33:37,599
Nobody's gonna die.

588
00:33:37,683 --> 00:33:39,518
- We're all gonna be okay.
- Everybody get some things.

589
00:33:39,601 --> 00:33:41,019
- We're getting out of here.
- Okay.

590
00:33:41,103 --> 00:33:42,688
Go. Come on. Get some things.

591
00:33:44,732 --> 00:33:45,733
Okay.

592
00:33:48,235 --> 00:33:50,821
Audrey, Brian, keep your heads down.

593
00:33:50,904 --> 00:33:52,614
Don't look out the windows.

594
00:33:52,698 --> 00:33:54,616
What about Starbuck?
Are we just leaving him?

595
00:33:54,700 --> 00:33:56,076
He'll be all right.

596
00:33:56,160 --> 00:33:57,369
We can't go looking for him right now.

597
00:33:57,453 --> 00:33:58,454
He'll be here when we get back.

598
00:34:10,424 --> 00:34:11,508
Oh, God.

599
00:34:12,301 --> 00:34:13,552
Shit.

600
00:34:13,635 --> 00:34:15,679
Why are we stopping?
What's happening?

601
00:34:15,763 --> 00:34:17,264
We're gonna go to Gladwin Street.

602
00:34:17,347 --> 00:34:18,766
There's got to be a way out of here.

603
00:34:43,165 --> 00:34:44,208
This is insane.

604
00:34:45,000 --> 00:34:46,210
Where the hell are we?

605
00:35:07,064 --> 00:35:08,148
It's okay.

606
00:35:08,232 --> 00:35:09,316
It's okay.

607
00:35:40,055 --> 00:35:41,056
Mom.

608
00:35:43,559 --> 00:35:44,560
Dad.

609
00:35:45,561 --> 00:35:47,062
What's gonna happen to us?

610
00:35:53,694 --> 00:35:55,028
- Got it?
- Yeah.

611
00:36:45,746 --> 00:36:47,956
You kind of smell like whiskey.

612
00:36:48,040 --> 00:36:49,249
Have you been...

613
00:36:49,333 --> 00:36:50,792
Oh, yeah.

614
00:36:50,876 --> 00:36:52,502
I might have had a little sip.

615
00:36:52,586 --> 00:36:54,838
I guess I needed to calm down.
You can smell it?

616
00:36:55,923 --> 00:36:56,924
Uh-huh.

617
00:37:07,851 --> 00:37:09,269
I wish you wouldn't drink.

618
00:37:09,353 --> 00:37:10,395
Not now.

619
00:37:13,357 --> 00:37:14,358
I need you here with me.

620
00:37:14,441 --> 00:37:15,609
Well, this is a lot to deal with.

621
00:37:15,692 --> 00:37:16,944
Greg, it started before we got here.

622
00:37:17,027 --> 00:37:18,320
Will you please be honest with me?

623
00:37:23,325 --> 00:37:24,326
I, uh...

624
00:37:25,911 --> 00:37:27,663
I was laid off a few weeks ago.

625
00:37:27,746 --> 00:37:31,041
I've been trying to find work,
doing part-time jobs for cash.

626
00:37:31,833 --> 00:37:32,960
Why didn't you tell me?

627
00:37:33,043 --> 00:37:34,127
- Well...
- Mom,

628
00:37:34,211 --> 00:37:35,462
where'd you put the other hammer?

629
00:37:36,964 --> 00:37:39,091
Could you just give us a minute, Brian?

630
00:37:39,174 --> 00:37:40,300
I didn't want you to worry.

631
00:37:41,969 --> 00:37:43,428
Well, that's just stupid.

632
00:37:43,512 --> 00:37:44,346
No, it's not. I--

633
00:37:44,429 --> 00:37:45,597
I need you to remember something.

634
00:37:45,681 --> 00:37:47,933
I can handle anything
you can handle, maybe more.

635
00:37:51,436 --> 00:37:53,689
Brian, find that other hammer?

636
00:37:53,772 --> 00:37:55,232
- No.
- It's in the garage.

637
00:37:55,315 --> 00:37:56,817
It has a yellow handle.

638
00:38:00,570 --> 00:38:01,947
Oh, Audrey, will you start bringing

639
00:38:02,030 --> 00:38:03,573
the supplies down to the basement?

640
00:38:03,657 --> 00:38:04,783
- Everything?
- Yeah, yeah.

641
00:38:04,866 --> 00:38:05,993
We're gonna sleep down there.

642
00:38:06,076 --> 00:38:07,244
It's the safest part of the house.

643
00:38:07,327 --> 00:38:08,578
Okay.

644
00:38:09,871 --> 00:38:10,872
Dad?

645
00:38:12,249 --> 00:38:14,209
What are we gonna do about Starbuck?

646
00:38:15,002 --> 00:38:16,169
Oh, buddy.

647
00:38:17,587 --> 00:38:20,340
I don't think we can do
anything right now.

648
00:38:20,424 --> 00:38:22,592
But Starbuck is a very smart dog.

649
00:38:22,676 --> 00:38:23,760
He'll be okay.

650
00:38:26,179 --> 00:38:28,056
You know he loves you so much.

651
00:38:29,099 --> 00:38:30,392
He'll find his way home.

652
00:38:30,475 --> 00:38:31,560
He will.

653
00:38:39,443 --> 00:38:42,654
- Dad?
- Yeah?

654
00:38:42,738 --> 00:38:44,364
The basement is totally flooded.

655
00:38:44,448 --> 00:38:45,782
- Oh, shit.
- What?

656
00:38:45,866 --> 00:38:47,576
We'll just have to use
the second floor, I guess.

657
00:38:56,293 --> 00:38:57,294
Damn it.

658
00:38:57,377 --> 00:38:59,004
Mom. What is it?

659
00:38:59,087 --> 00:39:00,172
Nothing.

660
00:39:00,964 --> 00:39:02,758
- Please tell me.
- I had--

661
00:39:02,841 --> 00:39:04,301
I had something very important down there.

662
00:39:04,384 --> 00:39:06,011
- What? What? What was it?
- It doesn't matter.

663
00:39:08,305 --> 00:39:09,473
Let's just keep this door closed

664
00:39:09,556 --> 00:39:11,141
and hope the water doesn't get
any higher, all right?

665
00:39:12,100 --> 00:39:13,810
Okay. I'm sorry, Mom.

666
00:39:13,894 --> 00:39:14,936
Thank you.

667
00:40:01,024 --> 00:40:02,526
This is the last of the milk.

668
00:40:03,819 --> 00:40:05,153
Well, we might as well finish it.

669
00:40:10,951 --> 00:40:12,035
Never gonna have milk again.

670
00:40:13,036 --> 00:40:14,121
Don't talk like that.

671
00:40:15,330 --> 00:40:17,040
Maybe dinosaurs have milk.

672
00:40:18,625 --> 00:40:19,709
Don't be stupid.

673
00:40:21,086 --> 00:40:23,547
I can't find any radio stations.

674
00:40:23,630 --> 00:40:25,632
Well, thanks for checking, buddy.

675
00:40:42,190 --> 00:40:43,233
Mom?

676
00:40:47,487 --> 00:40:49,489
Is this the end of the world?

677
00:40:53,785 --> 00:40:54,953
No.

678
00:40:55,495 --> 00:40:56,538
It's not.

679
00:40:58,039 --> 00:40:59,249
What is it then?

680
00:41:07,048 --> 00:41:08,842
I think that our neighborhood,

681
00:41:09,885 --> 00:41:11,094
our whole street...

682
00:41:13,680 --> 00:41:14,931
has moved.

683
00:41:17,309 --> 00:41:18,727
I think...

684
00:41:20,020 --> 00:41:23,648
our house is somewhere else now.

685
00:41:25,442 --> 00:41:26,526
Where?

686
00:41:29,613 --> 00:41:31,114
We're in the past.

687
00:41:33,783 --> 00:41:35,327
Aren't we?

688
00:41:35,410 --> 00:41:37,287
How the hell is that even possible?

689
00:41:37,370 --> 00:41:38,705
I don't know.

690
00:41:42,125 --> 00:41:43,460
It was the lights.

691
00:41:45,795 --> 00:41:47,422
What?

692
00:41:47,505 --> 00:41:49,507
The lights that Starbuck was barking at.

693
00:41:51,092 --> 00:41:52,385
The lights brought us here.

694
00:41:53,762 --> 00:41:54,804
Yeah, maybe.

695
00:41:55,889 --> 00:41:57,390
I mean, Sagan wrote about wormholes.

696
00:41:58,141 --> 00:41:59,226
The lights could be portals

697
00:41:59,309 --> 00:42:01,561
moving things between
different points in time.

698
00:42:03,396 --> 00:42:05,190
Like the plant at Mrs. Huddleston's?

699
00:42:05,273 --> 00:42:06,733
Or the shit in Mel's backyard.

700
00:42:06,816 --> 00:42:09,653
Maybe the lights carried those things

701
00:42:09,736 --> 00:42:10,987
from the past to the present.

702
00:42:11,696 --> 00:42:13,031
And us back to the past.

703
00:42:13,823 --> 00:42:14,824
How?

704
00:42:15,659 --> 00:42:17,494
Well...

705
00:42:17,577 --> 00:42:19,913
the portals could have acted as tremors.

706
00:42:19,996 --> 00:42:21,915
It's like barely noticeable at first.

707
00:42:21,998 --> 00:42:23,124
Swapping small sections of land

708
00:42:23,208 --> 00:42:25,543
between different points in time.

709
00:42:25,627 --> 00:42:28,964
And maybe the tremors grew
until the big one finally hit,

710
00:42:29,047 --> 00:42:31,007
and our whole neighborhood
got swapped out.

711
00:42:32,092 --> 00:42:34,135
Well, if that's true,

712
00:42:34,219 --> 00:42:36,680
then it could take us back home again.

713
00:42:36,763 --> 00:42:38,473
So, what? Are we just gonna wait here?

714
00:42:38,556 --> 00:42:39,891
- Greg.
- Yeah.

715
00:42:39,975 --> 00:42:42,894
Yeah. We're gonna survive.

716
00:42:42,978 --> 00:42:44,688
And we're gonna wait for
the lights to take us back.

717
00:42:44,771 --> 00:42:45,897
That's the plan.

718
00:42:45,981 --> 00:42:48,400
Dad, how do you know
that that's even gonna happen?

719
00:42:48,483 --> 00:42:49,484
We don't know.

720
00:42:49,567 --> 00:42:50,819
Well, I believe it will.

721
00:42:50,902 --> 00:42:51,987
How?

722
00:42:52,070 --> 00:42:53,196
I know.

723
00:42:53,947 --> 00:42:55,031
Because...

724
00:42:56,157 --> 00:42:58,118
God's not gonna let us die here.

725
00:42:58,201 --> 00:42:59,202
Greg,

726
00:42:59,286 --> 00:43:00,578
you only go to church at Christmas,

727
00:43:00,662 --> 00:43:01,997
and now you're telling the kids

728
00:43:02,080 --> 00:43:03,331
- God is looking out for us.
- What about the people...

729
00:43:03,415 --> 00:43:05,125
- You're being ridiculous.
- ...getting eaten by animals?

730
00:43:06,251 --> 00:43:07,335
I believe Dad.

731
00:43:10,297 --> 00:43:11,339
Okay.

732
00:43:11,923 --> 00:43:12,966
Good.

733
00:43:13,049 --> 00:43:15,802
If it makes you feel better, believe him.

734
00:43:17,178 --> 00:43:18,388
I'm just scared.

735
00:43:22,600 --> 00:43:23,977
And I don't want to lie to you.

736
00:44:26,331 --> 00:44:30,627
<i>♪ So wild, standing there ♪</i>

737
00:44:30,710 --> 00:44:32,796
<i>♪ With her hands in her hair ♪</i>

738
00:44:34,631 --> 00:44:39,219
<i>- ♪ I can't help remember ♪</i>
- <i>♪ ...help remember ♪</i>

739
00:44:39,302 --> 00:44:41,429
<i>- ♪ Just where she touched me ♪
- ♪ Just where she touched me ♪</i>

740
00:44:44,140 --> 00:44:46,893
<i>- ♪ There is still no face ♪
- ♪ There is still no face ♪</i>

741
00:44:48,395 --> 00:44:51,064
<i>♪ Here in her place ♪</i>

742
00:44:51,147 --> 00:44:52,941
<i>♪ So cool ♪</i>

743
00:44:53,024 --> 00:44:55,026
- ♪ ...<i>she was like ♪
- ♪ ...she was like ♪</i>

744
00:44:55,110 --> 00:44:57,112
<i>- ♪ Jazz on a summer's day ♪
- ♪ Jazz on a summer's day ♪</i>

745
00:44:59,406 --> 00:45:03,535
<i>- ♪ Music, high and sweet ♪
- ♪ Music, high and sweet ♪</i>

746
00:45:03,618 --> 00:45:05,620
<i>- ♪ Then she just blew away ♪
- ♪ Then she just blew away ♪</i>

747
00:45:08,790 --> 00:45:12,293
<i>♪ Now she can't be that warm ♪</i>

748
00:45:15,171 --> 00:45:17,048
<i>♪ With the wind ♪</i>

749
00:45:17,132 --> 00:45:18,925
<i>- ♪ In her arms ♪
- ♪ In her arms ♪</i>

750
00:45:19,008 --> 00:45:23,263
<i>- ♪ Valerie, call on me ♪
- ♪ Valerie, call on me ♪</i>

751
00:45:23,346 --> 00:45:27,308
<i>- ♪ Call on me, Valerie ♪
- ♪ Call on me, Valerie ♪</i>

752
00:45:27,392 --> 00:45:30,520
<i>♪ Come and see me ♪</i>

753
00:45:31,771 --> 00:45:34,858
<i>♪ I'm the same boy
I used to be ♪</i>

754
00:45:38,695 --> 00:45:40,363
I know you were
trying to comfort the kids,

755
00:45:40,447 --> 00:45:41,906
but we might be here forever.

756
00:45:41,990 --> 00:45:43,199
You know that, right?

757
00:45:43,283 --> 00:45:44,534
Well, I don't want to believe that.

758
00:45:44,617 --> 00:45:45,827
Of course not, but...

759
00:45:47,287 --> 00:45:50,123
We can't stay in the house indefinitely.

760
00:45:50,206 --> 00:45:52,667
Eventually, we're gonna need
more food, and water--

761
00:45:52,750 --> 00:45:54,669
We would be killed and eaten
if we go outside.

762
00:45:54,752 --> 00:45:57,714
- Is that what you want?
- There are other people here.

763
00:45:57,797 --> 00:45:59,174
Other families are trying to survive.

764
00:45:59,257 --> 00:46:00,967
The smart ones are gonna gather supplies.

765
00:46:01,050 --> 00:46:04,471
Water, food, guns, ammunition.

766
00:46:04,554 --> 00:46:06,764
Well, why don't we wait a few
days and see what happens?

767
00:46:06,848 --> 00:46:08,099
Okay, we can. We can.

768
00:46:11,311 --> 00:46:12,562
- Oh, God.
- What is that?

769
00:46:22,906 --> 00:46:23,948
Mom.

770
00:46:24,032 --> 00:46:25,116
It's okay.

771
00:46:25,200 --> 00:46:26,618
- What's going on?
- It's okay.

772
00:46:53,811 --> 00:46:55,897
Down, down, down.
Get down. Get down. Stay down.

773
00:46:55,980 --> 00:46:57,524
- Are you kidding?
- Are you okay?

774
00:46:59,859 --> 00:47:01,152
This is my house!

775
00:47:01,236 --> 00:47:03,154
Oh, my-- Oh, my God. It's Mel.

776
00:47:03,238 --> 00:47:04,405
He's on his roof.

777
00:47:04,489 --> 00:47:05,698
He's got a gun.

778
00:47:07,408 --> 00:47:09,452
- He's shooting at the dinosaurs?
- Yeah!

779
00:47:09,536 --> 00:47:11,496
Maybe that's a good thing.
He'll scare 'em away.

780
00:47:11,579 --> 00:47:13,456
- Or draw their attention!
- He's a damned idiot.

781
00:47:13,540 --> 00:47:15,500
I see you!

782
00:47:15,583 --> 00:47:18,169
I'm gonna send you back to extinction!

783
00:47:18,253 --> 00:47:20,255
- Oh, no! Get out of the room!
- Go! Go! Get out!

784
00:47:20,338 --> 00:47:23,174
- Kids, please!
- Okay. Okay.

785
00:47:23,258 --> 00:47:26,052
This is my house,
you sons of bitches!

786
00:47:26,135 --> 00:47:27,762
This is my house.

787
00:47:27,845 --> 00:47:30,223
This is my goddamn house.

788
00:47:30,306 --> 00:47:31,641
Ah!

789
00:47:35,562 --> 00:47:37,188
Oh! Ah!

790
00:47:39,023 --> 00:47:39,941
Get off!

791
00:47:40,024 --> 00:47:41,276
- No, no.
- No, no, no. Get off me!

792
00:47:41,359 --> 00:47:43,027
- No.
- Somebody help me!

793
00:47:45,572 --> 00:47:47,907
Help me!

794
00:48:12,307 --> 00:48:13,349
Greg?

795
00:48:13,433 --> 00:48:15,018
- Yeah?
- What are we gonna do?

796
00:48:15,101 --> 00:48:16,811
We can't live like this.

797
00:48:16,894 --> 00:48:18,396
There's got to be some way out of here.

798
00:48:18,479 --> 00:48:20,398
We just all have to stay together, and--

799
00:48:20,481 --> 00:48:21,733
How do you know that?

800
00:48:21,816 --> 00:48:23,818
What? Well, I don't know for
sure. It's just what I feel.

801
00:48:23,901 --> 00:48:25,778
Will you stop being so damn optimistic?

802
00:48:25,862 --> 00:48:27,864
This is not gonna be okay.

803
00:48:29,032 --> 00:48:30,700
Well, what the hell do you want me to do?

804
00:48:30,783 --> 00:48:33,161
I want you to be honest about
the situation. I want you...

805
00:48:33,244 --> 00:48:35,872
That we're stuck here
for the rest of our lives.

806
00:48:35,955 --> 00:48:36,956
That-- That-- That-- That--

807
00:48:37,040 --> 00:48:38,291
That we need to be honest with our kids

808
00:48:38,374 --> 00:48:41,461
- about what that means.
- Everything I do is wrong.

809
00:48:43,004 --> 00:48:45,965
All year, I've been trying
to keep this family together,

810
00:48:46,049 --> 00:48:48,134
and all you've wanted to do
is tear it apart.

811
00:48:48,217 --> 00:48:49,510
How can you say that?

812
00:48:50,595 --> 00:48:52,096
You never want to talk about anything

813
00:48:52,180 --> 00:48:53,348
or deal with anything.

814
00:48:53,431 --> 00:48:56,351
And you have been drinking
and lying about your job.

815
00:48:56,434 --> 00:48:58,519
How is that keeping the family
together, Greg?

816
00:48:58,603 --> 00:49:01,064
- I'm not the only one.
- How did I lie?

817
00:49:01,147 --> 00:49:02,940
All that typing in the basement!

818
00:49:03,733 --> 00:49:06,069
I read your book, Denise!

819
00:49:06,152 --> 00:49:09,113
You wanted to leave us for
a long time, me and the kids.

820
00:49:09,197 --> 00:49:11,240
That's-- No, that is not true!

821
00:49:11,324 --> 00:49:12,909
- Oh, no?
- No, it's just a story!

822
00:49:12,992 --> 00:49:15,119
Oh, bullshit. It reads
exactly like our life!

823
00:49:15,203 --> 00:49:16,371
No. You don't understand!

824
00:49:16,454 --> 00:49:18,247
- You don't understand!
- Oh, is this too much for you?

825
00:49:18,331 --> 00:49:19,624
Is this too much? You can't handle it?

826
00:49:19,707 --> 00:49:22,001
How do you think I feel? How
do you think the kids feel?

827
00:49:22,085 --> 00:49:25,546
- When did you stop loving us?
- Don't say that!

828
00:49:25,630 --> 00:49:27,131
You don't listen to me!

829
00:49:28,424 --> 00:49:30,093
You don't actually hear me!

830
00:49:31,969 --> 00:49:33,262
You don't listen to the words that come...

831
00:49:33,346 --> 00:49:35,181
- Starbuck!
- I'm just here.

832
00:49:38,267 --> 00:49:40,561
No, no, no, no! Starbuck!

833
00:49:40,645 --> 00:49:43,147
...making your whole life happen.

834
00:49:44,065 --> 00:49:45,650
You don't actually hear me!

835
00:49:50,196 --> 00:49:51,155
You nearly...

836
00:49:51,239 --> 00:49:52,407
And you think, "What does 'the me' want?

837
00:49:52,490 --> 00:49:53,700
How is 'the me'..."

838
00:49:53,783 --> 00:49:56,035
I'm the only person
that I think about?

839
00:49:56,119 --> 00:49:57,787
That's what you're supposed to say!

840
00:49:57,870 --> 00:49:59,747
Brian!

841
00:49:59,831 --> 00:50:01,666
Brian!

842
00:50:13,302 --> 00:50:14,345
Starbuck!

843
00:50:38,745 --> 00:50:39,787
Audrey?

844
00:50:47,462 --> 00:50:48,504
Audrey?

845
00:50:49,046 --> 00:50:50,131
Audrey!

846
00:50:51,466 --> 00:50:52,508
Brian?

847
00:50:53,426 --> 00:50:54,635
Greg! Greg!

848
00:51:01,350 --> 00:51:02,602
Where do you think they went?

849
00:51:02,685 --> 00:51:03,811
I don't know. I don't know.

850
00:51:03,895 --> 00:51:05,605
We'll find them. We'll find them.

851
00:51:05,688 --> 00:51:07,857
I can't believe they'd do this.

852
00:51:09,025 --> 00:51:10,067
Brian!

853
00:51:10,860 --> 00:51:11,903
Audrey!

854
00:51:16,949 --> 00:51:18,201
Starbuck!

855
00:51:26,042 --> 00:51:27,126
Starbuck!

856
00:51:42,099 --> 00:51:43,100
Shit.

857
00:51:45,561 --> 00:51:46,562
Brian!

858
00:52:07,875 --> 00:52:08,960
Kids!

859
00:52:09,961 --> 00:52:11,045
Audrey!

860
00:52:15,967 --> 00:52:17,301
What is that?

861
00:52:28,479 --> 00:52:30,064
What do I do?

862
00:52:30,147 --> 00:52:32,024
Just keep going. They'll get out the way.

863
00:52:35,862 --> 00:52:36,863
They're not moving.

864
00:52:36,946 --> 00:52:37,989
Oh, God.

865
00:52:40,116 --> 00:52:42,326
Maybe I could just drive around them?

866
00:52:42,410 --> 00:52:43,744
Tap the horn.

867
00:52:44,996 --> 00:52:46,747
What, we tell every animal
in the neighborhood

868
00:52:46,831 --> 00:52:48,541
- that we're here?
- All right. Well,

869
00:52:48,624 --> 00:52:50,126
drive up on the grass.

870
00:53:25,870 --> 00:53:29,457
- Greg!
- Reverse! Reverse! Go back!

871
00:53:29,540 --> 00:53:31,375
- Oh, my God. No, no, no.
- Oh, my God! Go!

872
00:53:31,459 --> 00:53:32,376
Greg!

873
00:53:32,460 --> 00:53:34,587
- Okay then-- Go, go, go!
- Oh, my God.

874
00:53:34,670 --> 00:53:37,423
No! Come on! Come on!

875
00:53:40,885 --> 00:53:41,969
Greg.

876
00:53:45,598 --> 00:53:47,224
- Greg!
- Oh, it's coming again!

877
00:53:47,308 --> 00:53:49,143
Oh, my God!

878
00:53:58,069 --> 00:53:59,236
Oh, Denise.

879
00:53:59,320 --> 00:54:00,363
Oh, God.

880
00:54:05,743 --> 00:54:07,411
Oh, God! Oh, God!

881
00:54:07,495 --> 00:54:09,455
Greg, go! Go! Go!

882
00:54:15,002 --> 00:54:15,962
Go!

883
00:54:46,575 --> 00:54:48,035
Starbuck!

884
00:54:54,291 --> 00:54:55,292
Starbuck?

885
00:55:13,561 --> 00:55:15,438
You thought it was funny
when you hurt my brother?

886
00:55:15,521 --> 00:55:16,439
No! No!

887
00:55:16,522 --> 00:55:17,523
Ow!

888
00:55:17,606 --> 00:55:18,941
When you broke his arm?

889
00:55:19,025 --> 00:55:20,776
- Stop! Stop it!
- I'm sorry, okay?

890
00:55:20,860 --> 00:55:22,319
Stop! You're gonna kill him!

891
00:55:22,403 --> 00:55:23,487
- Stop!
- He broke your arm!

892
00:55:23,571 --> 00:55:24,822
I didn't mean to.

893
00:55:24,905 --> 00:55:26,282
So what? Who cares?

894
00:55:26,365 --> 00:55:27,825
It doesn't matter anymore!

895
00:55:27,908 --> 00:55:28,993
Please!

896
00:55:29,076 --> 00:55:30,619
- I wanna kill him!
- Leave him alone!

897
00:55:30,703 --> 00:55:33,539
Stop! Get off him!
Please, leave him alone!

898
00:55:33,622 --> 00:55:35,750
Please! Leave him alone!

899
00:55:35,833 --> 00:55:38,294
Please!

900
00:55:39,712 --> 00:55:40,713
I'm sorry.

901
00:55:40,796 --> 00:55:43,340
Oh, God. I'm so sorry.

902
00:55:43,424 --> 00:55:45,634
I don't know what I'm doing.

903
00:55:45,718 --> 00:55:47,178
I don't know what's gonna happen to us.

904
00:55:47,261 --> 00:55:49,346
Come on. Let's go.

905
00:55:49,430 --> 00:55:51,390
Let's just try to find Mom.

906
00:55:51,474 --> 00:55:52,933
Let's go, please! Let's go!

907
00:56:25,633 --> 00:56:26,842
Oh, shit.

908
00:56:44,610 --> 00:56:46,070
Come on. Come on.

909
00:56:46,153 --> 00:56:47,404
Let's go.

910
00:56:47,488 --> 00:56:48,864
Okay. Come on.

911
00:56:58,457 --> 00:56:59,458
Oh, my God.

912
00:57:00,042 --> 00:57:01,252
Oh, my God.

913
00:57:01,335 --> 00:57:02,336
What happened?

914
00:57:02,419 --> 00:57:03,671
What happened?

915
00:57:03,754 --> 00:57:05,881
Oh, your face looks like
a pepperoni pizza.

916
00:57:05,965 --> 00:57:06,799
Leave me alone.

917
00:57:06,882 --> 00:57:08,592
I don't want to talk about it.

918
00:57:08,676 --> 00:57:10,427
Why did you run away?

919
00:57:10,511 --> 00:57:11,929
I saw Starbuck.

920
00:57:12,012 --> 00:57:13,931
He was by the house, but he's gone now.

921
00:57:14,557 --> 00:57:15,724
Where is he?

922
00:57:15,808 --> 00:57:16,892
I don't know. I can't find him.

923
00:57:17,601 --> 00:57:18,644
Oh, Brian.

924
00:57:19,854 --> 00:57:22,022
You know, he-- he might be...

925
00:57:22,106 --> 00:57:23,315
Don't say it.

926
00:57:25,860 --> 00:57:27,570
- Come on. Come on.
- Somebody help me!

927
00:57:27,653 --> 00:57:29,238
Somebody help me, please!

928
00:57:35,703 --> 00:57:36,787
Hey!

929
00:57:38,372 --> 00:57:39,582
Stay away from her!

930
00:57:45,671 --> 00:57:47,381
- Get away from her!
- Hey!

931
00:57:47,464 --> 00:57:49,341
Over here! Hey!

932
00:57:51,177 --> 00:57:52,636
Help me, please! Please!

933
00:58:03,856 --> 00:58:04,940
Hey.

934
00:58:05,024 --> 00:58:06,025
Where are you going?

935
00:58:07,318 --> 00:58:08,444
Wait.

936
00:58:08,527 --> 00:58:09,570
Come back!

937
00:58:10,279 --> 00:58:11,655
Wait.

938
00:58:14,575 --> 00:58:16,076
Leave me alone!

939
00:58:16,160 --> 00:58:17,453
We're not gonna hurt you.

940
00:58:19,955 --> 00:58:20,956
Are you okay?

941
00:58:22,875 --> 00:58:24,084
No.

942
00:58:24,168 --> 00:58:25,252
Are you alone?

943
00:58:28,756 --> 00:58:29,882
Your parents?

944
00:58:36,680 --> 00:58:37,723
I'm sorry.

945
00:58:44,355 --> 00:58:46,357
I'm sorry.

946
00:58:49,652 --> 00:58:50,861
What's your name?

947
00:58:51,445 --> 00:58:52,488
Jeannette.

948
00:58:52,571 --> 00:58:54,281
Okay, okay, I'm Audrey.

949
00:58:54,365 --> 00:58:55,658
And that's my brother, Brian.

950
00:58:56,283 --> 00:58:57,284
Hi.

951
00:58:58,869 --> 00:59:00,162
You can come with us.

952
00:59:01,580 --> 00:59:02,915
We'll find somewhere safe.

953
00:59:04,333 --> 00:59:05,334
Okay?

954
00:59:06,710 --> 00:59:07,878
Thank you.

955
00:59:10,214 --> 00:59:11,215
Brian!

956
00:59:14,343 --> 00:59:15,386
Audrey!

957
00:59:18,430 --> 00:59:20,057
Don't worry, Denise. We'll find them.

958
00:59:21,642 --> 00:59:22,726
They'll be okay.

959
00:59:45,332 --> 00:59:47,751
Go. Go. Go.

960
01:00:33,839 --> 01:00:34,965
What is it?

961
01:00:36,133 --> 01:00:38,385
I think it's the light
that Brian told us about.

962
01:01:52,459 --> 01:01:54,545
Maybe this'll take us back home.

963
01:01:54,628 --> 01:01:56,255
Back to our time.

964
01:01:56,338 --> 01:01:57,339
We need to find the kids

965
01:01:57,423 --> 01:01:59,007
and get back here as quick as we can.

966
01:01:59,091 --> 01:02:02,136
- You should go through it now.
- What are you talking about?

967
01:02:02,219 --> 01:02:03,929
I'll find the kids, and we'll
meet you on the other side.

968
01:02:04,012 --> 01:02:05,764
We go through together or not at all.

969
01:02:05,848 --> 01:02:07,558
I just want you to be safe.

970
01:02:07,641 --> 01:02:10,018
I'm not getting separated
from you and the kids.

971
01:02:20,487 --> 01:02:21,697
Whose house is this?

972
01:02:22,865 --> 01:02:24,741
I don't know, but I did find
some mercurochrome

973
01:02:24,825 --> 01:02:25,909
and some bandages.

974
01:02:29,329 --> 01:02:30,330
Jeannette?

975
01:02:31,707 --> 01:02:33,333
What was it like going to private school?

976
01:02:35,502 --> 01:02:36,920
I never went to public school,

977
01:02:37,004 --> 01:02:38,797
so I don't know how different it is.

978
01:02:40,174 --> 01:02:41,425
We don't pray at our school.

979
01:02:42,468 --> 01:02:44,803
Yeah, you can pray wherever you want.

980
01:02:44,887 --> 01:02:46,013
Nobody has to know.

981
01:02:47,639 --> 01:02:48,640
I guess that's true.

982
01:02:51,643 --> 01:02:53,061
Audrey, do you believe in God?

983
01:02:54,938 --> 01:02:56,148
Not really.

984
01:02:56,773 --> 01:02:57,816
I do.

985
01:02:57,900 --> 01:02:59,568
Yeah,
sometimes I don't either.

986
01:03:00,319 --> 01:03:01,820
Ah.

987
01:03:02,779 --> 01:03:03,822
Does it hurt?

988
01:03:03,906 --> 01:03:05,365
Yeah, a little bit.

989
01:03:06,033 --> 01:03:07,159
I'm sorry.

990
01:03:07,951 --> 01:03:08,952
It's okay.

991
01:03:19,630 --> 01:03:21,673
We gotta get home soon.

992
01:03:21,757 --> 01:03:23,091
Mom and Dad are gonna be so worried.

993
01:03:23,175 --> 01:03:24,510
Wait.

994
01:03:25,719 --> 01:03:26,803
Somebody's out there.

995
01:03:30,933 --> 01:03:32,017
Brian?

996
01:03:33,477 --> 01:03:34,478
Audrey?

997
01:03:36,230 --> 01:03:37,231
Mom!

998
01:03:37,314 --> 01:03:38,524
Dad!

999
01:03:40,692 --> 01:03:41,693
Oh, sweetie!

1000
01:03:41,777 --> 01:03:43,612
- Oh, we love you so much.
- Oh!

1001
01:03:43,695 --> 01:03:44,821
- So much.
- I'm so sorry, Mom.

1002
01:03:44,905 --> 01:03:46,532
- No, no, no, no. I'm so sorry.
- I'm so sorry.

1003
01:03:46,615 --> 01:03:48,700
- So happy you're still alive!
- That's okay.

1004
01:03:48,784 --> 01:03:49,785
- Come! Come!
- Come here.

1005
01:03:49,868 --> 01:03:51,078
- Dad! Dad.
- Son.

1006
01:03:51,161 --> 01:03:52,454
Oh, Brian.

1007
01:03:52,538 --> 01:03:53,872
Love you guys.

1008
01:03:53,956 --> 01:03:55,165
Mom. Dad.

1009
01:03:56,166 --> 01:03:57,167
This is Jeannette.

1010
01:03:57,251 --> 01:03:58,252
Hello.

1011
01:03:58,335 --> 01:03:59,711
Oh, hi, Jeannette.

1012
01:04:00,796 --> 01:04:02,506
She's all by herself.

1013
01:04:02,589 --> 01:04:03,966
She really needs someone to stay with.

1014
01:04:04,049 --> 01:04:05,926
- Well, she can stay with us.
- Yeah, of course she can.

1015
01:04:06,009 --> 01:04:07,719
- Take care of you.
- Thank you.

1016
01:04:07,803 --> 01:04:08,845
Oh, God.

1017
01:04:15,352 --> 01:04:18,397
Greg, we have to go
that way to get home.

1018
01:04:19,398 --> 01:04:20,440
I know.

1019
01:04:25,696 --> 01:04:26,989
I want you kids to get back in that house

1020
01:04:27,072 --> 01:04:28,490
and wait for us.

1021
01:04:28,574 --> 01:04:29,741
We're gonna make sure it's safe, okay?

1022
01:04:29,825 --> 01:04:30,909
- Okay, come on.
- Yeah. Hurry.

1023
01:04:30,993 --> 01:04:32,202
- Are you sure?
- Run, run, run.

1024
01:05:05,110 --> 01:05:06,445
Holy shit, they're doing it.

1025
01:05:10,782 --> 01:05:11,992
How is this funny?

1026
01:05:13,577 --> 01:05:14,953
I... I mean, it's...

1027
01:05:17,873 --> 01:05:19,082
Look at his...

1028
01:05:20,917 --> 01:05:22,127
You are silly.

1029
01:05:27,090 --> 01:05:28,884
I want to take a picture of you.

1030
01:05:28,967 --> 01:05:30,260
What?

1031
01:05:30,344 --> 01:05:31,678
Picture of you in front of them.

1032
01:05:31,762 --> 01:05:34,014
Denise, have you any idea
how much danger we're in?

1033
01:05:35,390 --> 01:05:37,225
Please just pose for my photo.

1034
01:05:37,309 --> 01:05:41,605
I want to remember
this insane, stupid moment.

1035
01:05:43,732 --> 01:05:45,067
Okay, hurry.

1036
01:05:45,150 --> 01:05:46,526
Take your crazy photo.

1037
01:05:47,903 --> 01:05:49,488
- Smile.
- Cheese.

1038
01:05:52,658 --> 01:05:54,117
- Can we go now?
- Yes.

1039
01:05:54,993 --> 01:05:56,078
Come on.

1040
01:06:03,126 --> 01:06:04,795
Maybe we should cut
through the Samuelsons' yard.

1041
01:06:04,878 --> 01:06:06,004
It might be faster.

1042
01:06:06,088 --> 01:06:07,297
No, this way is better.

1043
01:06:08,215 --> 01:06:09,424
Listen to your father.

1044
01:07:07,774 --> 01:07:08,900
Look at that.

1045
01:07:10,610 --> 01:07:11,862
Where'd the fire come from?

1046
01:07:11,945 --> 01:07:13,405
- Did we start that?
- Maybe.

1047
01:07:14,698 --> 01:07:15,866
We gotta get out of here.

1048
01:07:15,949 --> 01:07:18,034
Maybe we can find
another one of those portals.

1049
01:07:18,118 --> 01:07:20,078
Where do we even look? It all
seems so random, doesn't it?

1050
01:07:20,162 --> 01:07:21,371
Yeah.

1051
01:07:21,455 --> 01:07:23,457
When it gets dark, we need to
get up someplace high.

1052
01:07:23,540 --> 01:07:24,624
Look for the light.

1053
01:07:24,708 --> 01:07:26,460
Okay, I'm just trying to think
of someplace high.

1054
01:07:26,543 --> 01:07:28,211
Mom! Dad!

1055
01:07:30,005 --> 01:07:31,840
- Run!
- Oh, my God. Oh, my God.

1056
01:07:44,478 --> 01:07:45,479
Shit.

1057
01:07:48,732 --> 01:07:49,733
Help!

1058
01:07:57,324 --> 01:07:58,492
Help!

1059
01:08:03,288 --> 01:08:04,498
